.TH LIBRDP-SESSION-BROKER 8 "2026-07-19" "librdp 0.1.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-session-broker \- allocate and supervise managed X11 RDP sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-session-broker
[
.B --config
.I path
]
.B --desktop
.I command
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-session-broker
is the privileged policy and allocation process for managed X11 sessions. It
authenticates through a separate per-session supervisor, allocates displays
and runtime directories, then runs each desktop and RDP agent with the
authenticated account.
.PP
The process remains in the foreground and writes bounded key/value diagnostics
to standard error. Credentials are accepted only over local IPC and are not
valid configuration keys.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Load the administrative configuration from an absolute path. This option must
be first. Later command-line options override file values.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate the effective policy and exit without creating a socket, display or
session.
.PP
Configuration uses
.I key=value
lines. Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored. Files must be regular, owned by root or the broker account and not
writable by group or other users.
.PP
The accepted keys are:
.BR socket ,
.BR runtime-root ,
.BR supervisor ,
.BR agent ,
.BR xserver ,
.BR auth-service ,
.BR desktop ,
.BR bind ,
.BR security ,
.BR tls-cert ,
.BR tls-key ,
.BR allow-user ,
.BR allow-group ,
.BR allow-env ,
.BR max-sessions ,
.BR max-sessions-per-user ,
.BR first-display ,
.BR last-display ,
.BR idle-seconds ,
.BR max-duration-seconds ,
.BR socket-mode ,
.BR socket-group ,
.BR allow-standard-security ,
.BR allow-user-switch ,
.BR allow-input ,
.BR allow-clipboard ,
.BR allow-drive ,
.BR drive-read-only ,
.BR allow-reconnect ,
.BR persistent
and
.BR xvfb .
.PP
.BR allow-user ,
.B allow-group
and
.B allow-env
may repeat. Other keys may occur once. Boolean values accept
.BR 1 / 0 ,
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no
and
.BR on / off
without regard to letter case.
.SH PATH AND AUTHENTICATION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " path"
Set the local broker socket.
.TP
.BI --runtime-root " path"
Set the per-session runtime root.
.TP
.BI --supervisor " path"
Set the trusted supervisor executable.
.TP
.BI --agent " path"
Set the unprivileged session agent executable.
.TP
.BI --xserver " path"
Set the production X server executable.
.TP
.BI --desktop " command"
Set the absolute desktop or window-manager command.
.TP
.BI --auth-service " name"
Set the native host-authentication service.
.TP
.BI --allow-user " name"
Add an authenticated account to the allowlist.
.TP
.BI --allow-group " name"
Add a local group to the allowlist.
.TP
.BI --allow-env " name"
Permit one environment variable in user sessions.
.SH LISTENER AND SECURITY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --bind " address"
Set the address used by per-session listeners.
.TP
.BI --security " nla|tls|standard"
Set session listener security. NLA is the default.
.TP
.BI --tls-cert " path"
Set the absolute certificate path.
.TP
.BI --tls-key " path"
Set the absolute private-key path.
.TP
.B --allow-standard-security
Permit Standard Security.
.TP
.B --deny-standard-security
Deny Standard Security.
.SH RESOURCE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --max-sessions " count"
Set the global session limit.
.TP
.BI --max-sessions-per-user " count"
Set the per-account session limit.
.TP
.BI --first-display " number"
Set the first allocatable X display.
.TP
.BI --last-display " number"
Set the last allocatable X display.
.TP
.BI --idle-seconds " value"
Set the detached idle limit.
.TP
.BI --max-duration-seconds " value"
Set the absolute session lifetime.
.TP
.BI --socket-mode " octal"
Set an owner-readable and owner-writable local socket mode with no access for
other users.
.TP
.BI --socket-group " name"
Set the optional local socket group.
.SH POLICY OPTIONS
.TP
.B --allow-user-switch
Permit a privileged caller to authenticate a different local account.
.TP
.B --deny-user-switch
Deny local account switching.
.TP
.B --allow-input
Permit requested remote input.
.TP
.B --deny-input
Deny remote input.
.TP
.B --allow-clipboard
Permit requested clipboard integration.
.TP
.B --deny-clipboard
Deny clipboard integration.
.TP
.B --allow-drive
Permit requested client-drive integration.
.TP
.B --deny-drive
Deny client-drive integration.
.TP
.B --drive-read-only
Restrict permitted drives to read-only access.
.TP
.B --drive-read-write
Permit write requests when the session also requests drive access.
.TP
.B --allow-reconnect
Permit reconnect tokens and detach.
.TP
.B --no-reconnect
Deny reconnect.
.TP
.B --persistent
Permit sessions to survive detach and broker replacement.
.TP
.B --non-persistent
Terminate sessions according to the nonpersistent policy.
.TP
.B --xorg
Use the configured production X server.
.TP
.B --xvfb
Use Xvfb for deterministic test environments.
.TP
.B --help
Print command usage.
.SH SERVICE OPERATION
A service manager should validate configuration before startup, run the broker
in the foreground, treat creation of the configured Unix socket as readiness
and forward
.B SIGTERM
for orderly shutdown. The broker also handles
.B SIGINT
and
.BR SIGHUP ;
these signals stop the process rather than reloading policy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/librdp/session-broker.sock
Default broker control socket.
.TP
.I /run/librdp/sessions
Default managed-session runtime root.
.TP
.I share/librdp/librdp-session-broker.conf.example
Installed configuration example.
.PP
.B librdp-session-supervisor
and
.B librdp-session-agent
are private helpers installed below the librdp libexec directory. The broker
starts the supervisor, which authenticates one account and starts the agent
under that account. They are not administrative commands and must not be
placed on a general command search path.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Records use the prefix
.B librdp x11-session-broker
and an
.B event=
field. Configuration rejection reports only line, key and reason. It never
reports the rejected value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp-server (1),
.BR librdp-server (7),
.BR librdp (7)
